  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Canopy Club in Urbana, Illinois, on Wednesday, October 12, 2005 [1]. This recording, taped by Peter Sohriakoff, captures a 43-minute set consisting of fourteen songs [1]. The performance opens with “Broom People” and “You or Your Memory” before moving into “The Monkey Song” [1]. This track is notable as the first appearance of the song in thirty-two archived shows, a span of 746 days [2]. The setlist continues with “International Small Arms Traffic Blues” and “Southwood Plantation Road” [1]. Next, the band plays “Spilling Toward Alpha,” a rare performance with only six archived instances, and its first appearance in forty-nine archived shows, a gap of 1,315 days [2]. “Cheshire County” follows, leading into “Neon Orange Glimmer Song” [1]. This song marks its first appearance in twenty-five archived shows, a period of 589 days [2]. The main set concludes with “Twin Human Highway Flares,” “Dance Music,” “Dilaudid,” and “This Year” [1]. After an encore break, during which Peter praises Urbana, Illinois, the band performs “It Froze Me” and “See America Right” [1]. This is the eighty-first show in the archive’s collection of four hundred and sixty-seven recordings for the performer [2]. The previous archived show took place on July 4, 2005, at Fulton Mall Parking Garage [2]. This is the only available recording of the event, making it a complete document of the night [1].",
